-- what is wrong after a change: every check that fails in the files it touches, and every such file the
-- machine did not read to the end. A change is kept only when nothing is: a failure is never carried
-- forward because it was there before (2026-11-18: lib/derive.cub's 24 failures had been carried for nine
-- days, and experiments/isa/addw-all.cub's refusal of jae-c under an out-of-memory)
hy-wrong : List (Bool × List (List Word)) → List (List Word)
hy-wrong nil = nil
hy-wrong (cons a as) = list-append (if fst a then snd a else cons "(the machine did not read to the end)" nil) (hy-wrong as)
